{"content":[{"c":["PEOPLE OF THE EAST*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Tribes located east and northeast of Canaan, many of them overtly hostile to the Jews. ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.29.1","r":"Gen.29.1","rawR":"Gen.29.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.29.1","value":"Gen.29.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 29:1"}," provides the first reference to these peoples. Jacob, en route to Haran, crossed through territory designated as “the land of the people of the east.”"],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The comprehensiveness of the term is evident in the way it is used to refer to nomads (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.25.10","r":"Ezek.25.10","rawR":"Ezek.25.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.25.10","value":"Ezek.25.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 25:10"},") or Mesopotamians (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.30","r":"1Kgs.4.30","rawR":"1Kgs.4.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.30","value":"1Kgs.4.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:30"},"). The term also occurs in association with specific tribes, such as the Amalekites (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.6.3","r":"Judg.6.3","rawR":"Judg.6.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.6.3","value":"Judg.6.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 6:3"},"), Ammonites (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.25.4","r":"Ezek.25.4","rawR":"Ezek.25.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.25.4","value":"Ezek.25.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 25:4"},"), Edomites (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.11.14","r":"Isa.11.14","rawR":"Isa.11.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.11.14","value":"Isa.11.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 11:14"},"), Kedarites (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.49.28","r":"Jer.49.28","rawR":"Jer.49.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.49.28","value":"Jer.49.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 49:28"},"), Midianites (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.6.33","r":"Judg.6.33","rawR":"Judg.6.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.6.33","value":"Judg.6.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 6:33"},"), and Moabites (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.25.10","r":"Ezek.25.10","rawR":"Ezek.25.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.25.10","value":"Ezek.25.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 25:10"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The most distinguished OT personality linked to the term is the patriarch Job, who is called the greatest man among all the people of the east (",{"href":"?bref=Job.1.3","r":"Job.1.3","rawR":"Job.1.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.1.3","value":"Job.1.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 1:3"},"). Job’s homeland, the land of Uz, was probably in the vicinity of Edom to the southeast of the Dead Sea."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"PeopleoftheEast","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Genesis 29:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.29.1","rawQueryValue":"Gen.29.1","sourceRefExact":"Gen.29.1"},{"anchorText":"Ez 25:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.25.10","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.25.10","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.25.10"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.30","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.30","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.30"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 6:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.6.3","rawQueryValue":"Judg.6.3","sourceRefExact":"Judg.6.3"},{"anchorText":"Ez 25:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.25.4","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.25.4","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.25.4"},{"anchorText":"Is 11:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.11.14","rawQueryValue":"Isa.11.14","sourceRefExact":"Isa.11.14"},{"anchorText":"Jer 49:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.49.28","rawQueryValue":"Jer.49.28","sourceRefExact":"Jer.49.28"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 6:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.6.33","rawQueryValue":"Judg.6.33","sourceRefExact":"Judg.6.33"},{"anchorText":"Ez 25:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.25.10","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.25.10","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.25.10"},{"anchorText":"Jb 1:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.1.3","rawQueryValue":"Job.1.3","sourceRefExact":"Job.1.3"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"56248c84f5a70eb74071ea39eb08aa0c0c8b3a6ae0629d4b394c3f3fd9a85efc","sourceItemName":"PeopleoftheEast","sourceItemOrder":108,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"PeopleoftheEast","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"People of the East*","title":"People of the East*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}